<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elisedd ap Gwylog</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Eliseg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elisedd ap Gwylog was a king of Powys in the first half of the 8th century. He is known chiefly from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pillar-of-eliseg">Pillar of Eliseg</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llangollen">Llangollen</a>, erected by his great-grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyngen-ap-cadell">Cyngen ap Cadell</a>, whose inscription records that Elisedd won back land from the English with fire and sword. The nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valle-crucis-abbey">Valle Crucis Abbey</a> takes its name from the pillar.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elisedd-ap-gwylog.jpg" alt="Elisedd ap Gwylog" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wolfgang Sauber · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elisegs_Pfeiler_5_S%C3%BCdost.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
